  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Madhav Raj (In- Person) vs The State Of Bihar on 31 January, 2026 In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Civil Writ Jurisdiction Case No.1142 of 2026 ====================================================== Madhav Raj (In- Person) ... ... Peti Versus The State of Bihar ... ... Respondent/s = = = = = = Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr.Madhav Raj (In Person) For the Respondent/s : Mr.P.K. Veram, Sr. Advocate Aag 3 Mr.Sanjay Kumar, Ac to Aag 3 == = = = ================= = ======================= CORAM: HONOURABLE THE CHIEF JUSTICE and HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE BIBEK CHAUDHURI ORAL ORDER (Per: HONOURABLE THE CHIEF JUSTICE) 2 31-01-2026 1.",
    "facts": "ii. To direct the Respondent Authorities to provide/give list of private hostels running in Patna High Court CWJC No.1142 of 2026(2) dt.31-01-2026 the State of Bihar without the permission of the authorities and are not registered under THE SARAIS ACT, 1867 and without complying with other requirements i.e. No Objection Certificates from Fire Services, Electricity Board, and Pollution Control Board etc. iii. To direct the respondent authorities to take necessary steps to close all the private hostels specially the girl's hostels running without registration/valid license and without permission of the concerned authorities for securing/preventing sexual, physical and other violence against them inside the hostel premises.",
    "arguments": "This writ petition has been filed by the Petitioner, Mr. Madhav Raj, who is learned counsel for this Court, seeking for following reliefs:- \"i. To direct the Respondent Authorities to form a regulatory body for effective regulation of private hostels in the State of Bihar to protect the students from any sort of harassment and exploitation and further for uniform rules for operations, staffing, and service quality across all private hostels, ensuring consistency.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "This writ petition has been filed by the Petitioner, Mr. Madhav Raj, who is learned counsel for this Court, seeking for following reliefs:- \"i. To direct the Respondent Authorities to form a regulatory body for effective regulation of private hostels in the State of Bihar to protect the students from any sort of harassment and exploitation and further for uniform rules for operations, staffing, and service quality across all private hostels, ensuring consistency.",
